(*
expect:
foreign ticks 0
done
*)
(* THE TIMER FOOTGUN THAT COST A NIGHT (2026-07-23/24, tuvm#94).

   `platform timers` answers a **fresh Timers instance on every call**, and each
   instance owns its own `pending` registry (token -> chan/msg). `Timers>>dispatch:`
   does `pending at: tokenEvent ifAbsent: [nil]` and, finding nothing, **silently
   returns** — no raise, no log, no crash.

   So a node that registers its timer on one instance and dispatches `sys/timer` on
   another gets a timer that is armed in C, fires correctly, posts correctly — and is
   then dropped on the floor. The observable is TOTAL SILENCE, which is
   indistinguishable from a hung board. A MagTag clock ran 9h23m overnight and struck
   ZERO of ~19 expected bells this way; the bug was in the node, not the timer.

   This test pins the negative: `good` is the dispatching instance and registers
   NOTHING, so its `pending` is empty; a timer registered on a *foreign* instance
   fires in C and delivers nothing. If a future change makes a foreign registration
   deliverable (or makes the drop loud), this test is the one that must be revisited.

   The positive case — one held instance, register and dispatch on it — is
   `06_timers.nsl`, which is why this file only needs the negative. Determinism via
   the host virtual clock (`advanceMillis:`), never wall time.

   Note also, for anyone tempted to "just use two instances": each fresh Timers starts
   `nextToken ::= 1`, so two instances hand out COLLIDING tokens. Even if dispatch
   found an entry it could be the wrong one. One instance per registry is the only
   coherent rule. *)
class TimersInstanceIdentity packageUsing: manifest = ( | ticks ::= 0. | ) (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space good ping |
    space:: platform space.
    (* `good` is the DISPATCHER, and deliberately registers nothing. *)
    good:: platform timers.
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :e | good dispatch: e ].
    ping:: space channel: 'ping'.
    ping whenever: '' do: [ :m | ticks:: ticks + 1 ].

    (* FOREIGN registration — a different Timers instance owns this token. *)
    (platform timers) every: 30 post: #o on: ping.

    platform advanceMillis: 300. space drain.
    ('foreign ticks ' , ticks printString) out.
    'done' out.
  )
) : (
)
